# Files excluded from semgrep scans. Paths relative to repo root.
#
# Rule of thumb: list directories that ship upstream-owned C/C++/Python we
# don't author or modify — semgrep findings there would be noise we can't
# act on without diverging from upstream.

# The Netflix-upstream MATLAB MEX helpers under compat/python-vmaf/matlab/
# are deliberately NOT listed. The entry that stood here was added on
# 2026-05-28 because the ADR-0700 rename (python/vmaf/ → compat/python-vmaf/)
# moved the tree out from under the old `python/vmaf/matlab/` line and
# vmaf-no-strcpy-strcat-sprintf started firing on it. The one call it covered
# — a `sprintf` whose result was passed to mexErrMsgTxt in
# MEX/innerProd.c — was replaced by a bounded snprintf in bc00da0be, so from
# then on the entry only hid the tree from every future finding. Those sources
# now scan clean, and ADR-1142 makes upstream origin a non-reason for an
# exemption in the first place.
# scripts/ci/tests/test_semgrep_vendored_scope.py fails if either path
# comes back here, in a rule-level exclude, or in the semgrep-local hook.

# Netflix-upstream Python training resource tree (datasets, param/feature
# dicts). Not C/C++; included here for completeness since semgrep's Python
# rules could fire on the same upstream drift ruff is silenced on.
# Paths updated for ADR-0700 rename:
python/vmaf/resource/
compat/python-vmaf/resource/

# Standard exclusions — third-party / generated.
subprojects/
build/
dist/
core/test/data/
model/
testdata/

# pre-push-mkdocs-strict.sh is itself a hook; it documents the SKIP= /
# --no-verify bypass patterns as user-facing help text in comments and a
# heredoc error message.  The vmaf-no-skip-hooks-in-scripts rule correctly
# flags scripts that programmatically invoke those bypasses, but this file
# is exempt: it is the hook being bypassed, not a caller that bypasses it.
scripts/git-hooks/pre-push-mkdocs-strict.sh

# scripts/githooks/pre-commit.sh is the native-bash hook (ADR-0924). Line 33
# contains a comment explaining the --no-verify escape hatch for users; it is
# documentation, not a programmatic bypass. The vmaf-no-skip-hooks-in-scripts
# rule fires on the comment's literal text; exempt this file the same way we
# exempt pre-push-mkdocs-strict.sh above.
scripts/githooks/pre-commit.sh

# Vendored cJSON (core/src/mcp/3rdparty/cJSON/) is deliberately NOT listed.
# ADR-0621 once ignored the whole file over three upstream TODO/FIXME markers,
# which also hid it from the banned-function rule; the cJSON 1.7.19 re-vendor
# then reintroduced eleven banned calls unnoticed. Vendored code is in scope
# (ADR-0683, ADR-1142); scripts/ci/tests/test_semgrep_vendored_scope.py fails
# if this file or a rule-level exclude hides that tree again.

# Binary / data suffixes.
*.pkl
*.mexa64
*.mexw64
*.mexmaci64
*.onnx
*.bin
*.yuv
*.npy
